     "text": "```python\nfrom pedantic import count_calls\n\n@count_calls\ndef h_index(citations):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the h-index for a given list of citations.\n\n    The h-index is defined as the maximum value h such that a researcher has\n    at least h papers that each have at least h citations.\n\n    Args:\n        citations (list of int): A list of integers representing the number of citations\n                                 each paper has received.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The h-index of the researcher.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Sort the citations in descending order\n    citations.sort(reverse=True)\n    \n    # Initialize h-index to 0\n    h = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through the sorted citations\n    for i, citation in enumerate(citations):\n        # Check if the current citation count is at least i + 1\n        if citation >= i + 1:\n            h = i + 1\n        else:\n            # If the citation count is less than the current position, break the loop\n            break\n    \n    return h\n```",
